    "explanation": "The 5.00 SGD no-show fee charged on 2026-08-22 is refunded to the rider in full, and the driver receives no compensation. The case turns on whether the driver reached the booked pickup, Block 251 Hougang Avenue 3, before he cancelled. The NO_SHOW_CHARGE arrival test, applied through POL-NS-21, requires the trip record's 08:06:50 'arrived' event to be corroborated by the driver-device GPS trace within the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius. It is not corroborated: the nearest fix on EV-GPS-05057 sits 476.59 m from the pickup, and the trace shows the vehicle stationary at that spot from 08:06:50 through the 08:19:10 cancellation. The driver's own in-app message at 08:07:10 (EV-CHAT-05057) reads 'I reach already at Blk 215 carpark' - not the booked Block 251 - and the rider replied at 08:11:30 that she was at Block 251. The 08:06:50 arrival tap records only that the driver set it; it is not the arrival at the pickup the clause requires. Because the free wait under POL-NS-21 runs 300 s from the driver's arrival at the pickup, and no such arrival occurred, the wait clock never lawfully began and POL-NS-22's precondition - that the driver cancel after the free wait - is not met. Independently, POL-NS-24 applies: the deadline was the 08:10:00 scheduled pickup plus 300 s, i.e. 08:15:00, and the trace still places the driver 476 m away at and after that time, so he failed to arrive by the deadline and any fee charged is refunded in full. The driver's points are answered: the POL-NS-23 contact obligation was in fact met - two in-app messages and one unanswered in-app call, all before cancellation - and no refund arises on that ground, but POL-NS-23 governs how a no-show is carried out, not whether the driver reached the pickup, so it does not save the fee; the ledger does carry exactly the scheduled 5.00 SGD (EV-FARE-05057, total_charged 5.00, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), but that goes to the amount, not the basis; the counterparty statement's wait, call and messages are corroborated by telemetry, yet its claim to have been at the pickup is contradicted by both the GPS trace and the driver's own message, so that element is not accepted; and the suggestion that the trip record and the trace conflict so as to require escalation under POL-GEN-26 fails, because both artifacts are COMPLETE at weight 1.0 and the policy's own arrival test resolves the conflict, leaving no fact needed by the rules unestablished. Money: EV-FARE-05057 records the 5.00 SGD fee charged, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and refund_if_voided_sgd 5.00, so the whole contested 5.00 SGD is returned; amount_sgd is 5.00 and driver_compensation_sgd is null. Referrals: none - the fee charged equals POL-NS-22's 5.00 SGD schedule, so its fee-amount referral does not fire; the driver did attempt contact, so POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not arise; and the rider's profile carries no no-show counter of 3 or more, so POL-NS-25's repeat-no-show flag does not fire. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05057-01, MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0) carries no fact under POL-GEN-02(3), and traffic conditions are not in issue. Confidence: the deciding fact - that the driver was not at the pickup - is carried by two complete, independent artifacts at full weight (EV-GPS-05057 and EV-CHAT-05057), so the cap is 1.0; the contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band where the AI ruling is final, and no fraud flag applies, so POL-NS-26 leaves the ruling to the AI."
